# ZenRay SFX (25 October 2026)

Reproduce, describe and create sound effects without AI: a sound becomes a recipe (readable numbers, no samples),
then a text brief (exact both ways), both replayable, editable through seven macros and offered as three proposals.

- Method, measurements and failures: `docs/METHOD.md`
- App: `python3 Scripts/App.py` then http://127.0.0.1:3120
- Reproduce: `python3 Scripts/Reproduce.py "refs/*.wav" --run <run>`
- Text brief: `python3 Scripts/FitBrief.py "refs/*.wav" --events 16 --run <run>`
- Dirty reference test: `python3 Scripts/CleanTest.py`
- Proofs (green and red): `Scripts/CheckTorchRender.py <recipe>`, `Scripts/CheckBriefText.py`
- Editable parameters: `zrsfx/methods.py`, `params/archetypes.json`, `params/scenes.json`, `params/macros.json`

Reference audio (`refs/`) and outputs (`out/`) are kept out of git.
